## Another Day, Another Contaminated Batch

509 recalls this year and counting--an unsettling stat that highlights just how precarious the state of our food supply remains. The culprit behind the latest uproar? Milk powder contaminated with Salmonella, supplied by California Dairies. So far, this mishap has led to a chain reaction, affecting products from well-known names like Legacy Bakehouse LLC and PS Seasoning & Spices, Inc.

### What's on the Chopping Block?

In the past week, 9 recalls have been recorded, mostly stemming from the same issue. Legacy Bakehouse LLC, for instance, has pulled products including Butter Parsley Bagel Crisps and Parmesan & Herb Bagel Crisps, while PS Seasoning & Spices yanked their Ellsworth Sour Cream + Onion Seasoning. All these products share a common thread: the use of contaminated milk powder.

### Behind the Numbers

With over 150 Class I recalls this year, it's clear that food safety remains an uphill battle. The fact that a single ingredient can cause such widespread repercussions is a sobering reminder of how interconnected the food supply chain is. Not to pile on, but when firms like Ghirardelli Chocolate Company and Albertsons also make the list of repeat offenders, you start to wonder if enough is being done to prevent these issues at the source.

### The Takeaway

While it's easy to point fingers at individual brands, the issue really boils down to systemic vulnerabilities. From ingredient sourcing to final product shelfing, the food industry has a long way to go in ensuring that safety is more than just a checkbox on a compliance form. Until then, we'll keep our eyes peeled and our pantry stocked--carefully.
